      "score": 25,
      "comments": 1,
      "author": "dsr",
      "published": "2026-08-06T11:37:30Z",
      "bullets": [
        "DOS COM executables lack structural headers and load directly into memory at offset 0x0100, enabling raw byte sequence execution.",
        "Constraining 16-bit x86 opcodes to printable ASCII characters allows source code or text files to function as valid binaries.",
        "Polyglot executables exploit flexible parsing rules, requiring security analysts to use deep binary inspection rather than simple file extensions."
      ]
    },
    {
